# Canonical policy

The monorepo root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) is the **source of truth** for all agents (Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, etc.).

Before non-trivial work:

1. Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and the domain row in [`docs/WAYFINDER.md`](../../docs/WAYFINDER.md).
2. Read [`.agents/knowledge/index.md`](../../.agents/knowledge/index.md) for relevant skills.
3. Append a row to [`docs/REPO-CHANGE-INDEX.md`](../../docs/REPO-CHANGE-INDEX.md) before declaring done.

## Two-layer policy

Product code lives in `apps/` and `packages/`. Agent infrastructure (`.cursor/`, `.agents/`, `.claude/`) must **never** become a runtime dependency of product code.

## Portal specifics

When working in `apps/portal/`, also read [`apps/portal/AGENTS.md`](../../apps/portal/AGENTS.md) and [`apps/portal/CLAUDE.md`](../../apps/portal/CLAUDE.md).

- Edge auth: `apps/portal/src/proxy.ts` (not `middleware.ts`)
- ACL single source of truth: `@repo/acl`
- Design system: [`docs/design-system/RULES.md`](../../docs/design-system/RULES.md)

## Quality gates (mandatory before done)

```bash
pnpm exec turbo run lint type-check test --force   # MUST show 0 cached
pnpm gates
pnpm format:check
```

Do not trust a non-forced `pnpm quality` — turbo can return a stale lint PASS.
